# La stanza di Lethe: cosa dicono le cose (vedi il vault, "La stanza di Lethe").
# Ogni cue ha il nome del tile dell'oggetto (room_layout.gd): un oggetto con un cue qui
# diventa interagibile da solo. "Lethe:" = i suoi pensieri (col ritratto), il resto è
# il narratore. Stato: truth / lies (GameState), seen("id") = quante volte ci ha già parlato.

~ covered_mirror
if seen("covered_mirror") == 0
	A mirror, under a bedsheet. One corner of the glass is uncovered.
	- Look into the corner.
		A sliver of an eye looks back. Tired. Red.
		Lethe: ...That's me.
		set truth += 1
	- It's just old furniture.
		Lethe: Just old furniture. Nothing to see here.
		set lies += 1
else
	The sheet hasn't moved. The corner is still there.
=> END

~ wall_calendar
Days crossed out, one by one, up to a circled day.
After that, nothing.
Lethe: I stopped counting.
=> END

~ food_tray
if seen("food_tray") == 0
	A tray by the door. The food is cold. Untouched.
	There's a note under the cup, with a little heart in the corner.
	- Read the note.
		"Please eat something. I'm not angry. I'll be right outside."
		Lethe: ...
	- Leave it.
		Lethe: Later.
else
	The food is still there. So is the note.
=> END

~ door
The door. Locked from the inside.
Lethe: Not yet.
=> END

~ nightstand
A photo frame, face down.
Lethe: Leave it like that.
=> END

~ paper_balls
Crumpled pages. Every one starts the same way: "I'm sorry for"
Lethe: For what? I never get past that line.
=> END

~ dead_plant
A plant nobody has watered in months.
Lethe: It was green, once. Wasn't it?
=> END

~ window
The moon, between the curtains.
Lethe: Out there, everything keeps going.
=> END

~ wall_poster
A poster of a magical girl. Her favourite, once.
Lethe: She never ran away from anything.
=> END

~ console
The console is still warm.
Lethe: One more game. Then I'll sleep.
She says that every night.
=> END

~ cushion
A cushion, pressed flat. Someone has sat here for a long time.
=> END

~ desk_pc
The screen glows. Unread messages pile up in a corner.
Lethe: I'll answer tomorrow.
=> END

~ bed
The bed is unmade.
Lethe: I'm not tired.
=> END

~ shelf
Little heroines on the shelf, all facing the room.
Lethe: Stop looking at me like that.
=> END

~ clothes
A jacket, thrown on the floor. It hasn't been outside in a long time.
=> END

~ trash_bag
A trash bag, tied shut. Nobody takes it out.
=> END
